## Overview of the flow

`POST /api/owners` → Spring Security filter chain → `@Valid` bean validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` → `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)` (which runs the `@PreAuthorize` check, then a long chain of manual validations, normalizations, duplicate checks, and derived-field computations) → `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner(...)` (transactional) → `OwnerRepository.save(...)` (Spring Data JPA) → JPA/Hibernate persist (enforcing the entity's own Bean Validation constraints) → audit log line → mapped back to `OwnerDto` and returned with `201 Created`.

Note there are **two** owner controllers, but only V1 handles `POST /api/owners` (`addOwner`). V2 (`OwnerRestControllerV2`) only implements `GET` paging (`listOwnersPage`), so it is not part of the create flow.

---

## 1. The controller method handling POST /api/owners

**Route definition (generated interface):** `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/api/OwnersApi.java`

The mapping lives on the generated `OwnersApi` interface that the controller implements. `PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners"` and, combined with the controller's `@RequestMapping("/api")`, yields `POST /api/owners`. The request body is validated here via `@Valid @RequestBody`:

```java
String PATH_ADD_OWNER = "/owners";
...
@RequestMapping(
    method = RequestMethod.POST,
    value = OwnersApi.PATH_ADD_OWNER,
    produces = { "application/json" },
    consumes = { "application/json" }
)
default ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(
    @Parameter(name = "OwnerFieldsDto", description = "The pet owner", required = true) @Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto
) { ... }
```

The interface is annotated `@Validated` (class level) which, together with the `@Valid` on the body parameter, triggers Bean Validation of the DTO **before** the controller body runs.

**Controller implementation:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`

Class declaration and constants (lines 61-126). Key: `@RestController`, `@RequestMapping("/api")`, `@CrossOrigin`, implements `OwnersApi`. It holds several static constants used by the create logic (disposable email domains, address abbreviations, national-number lengths, region postcode ranges) and a dedicated `AUDIT` logger.

The actual handler is `addOwner` (lines 153-273). It carries `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")` and `@Override`:

```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    // Validate & normalize the optional email; reject the create when it is present but invalid.
    if (!normalizeEmail(ownerFieldsDto)) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    // Validate & normalize the optional postcode; reject the create when it is present but
    // not valid for the owner's city (see normalizePostcode).
    if (!normalizePostcode(ownerFieldsDto)) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    // Normalize the required address ...
    String canonicalAddress = normalizeAddress(ownerFieldsDto.getAddress());
    if (canonicalAddress.isBlank()) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    ownerFieldsDto.setAddress(canonicalAddress);
    // Reject the create when the owner's city is already at capacity (>= 50 owners).
    if (countOwnersInCity(ownerFieldsDto.getCity()) >= 50) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
    }
    // Normalize the telephone to E.164; reject when it cannot form a valid number.
    String normalizedTelephone = toE164(ownerFieldsDto.getTelephone());
    if (normalizedTelephone == null) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    ownerFieldsDto.setTelephone(normalizedTelephone);
    // Consolidated duplicate detection via identity key.
    Owner candidate = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    String contactIdentity = identityContact(candidate);
    boolean identityInUse = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
        .anyMatch(existing -> contactIdentity.equals(identityContact(existing)));
    if (identityInUse) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
    }
    // Household duplicate detection keyed on householdId.
    String householdId = ownerMapper.householdId(candidate);
    boolean householdExists = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()
        .anyMatch(existing -> householdId.equals(ownerMapper.householdId(existing)));
    boolean sharesHousehold = Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold());
    if (householdExists && !sharesHousehold) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
    }
    boolean declaredMember = householdExists && sharesHousehold;
    // Determine effective registration date (supplied or today), reject future dates,
    // roll forward to next business day.
    LocalDate registrationDate = ownerFieldsDto.getRegistrationDate();
    if (registrationDate == null) {
        registrationDate = LocalDate.now();
    }
    else if (registrationDate.isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    registrationDate = toBusinessDay(registrationDate);
    // Reject when daily sign-up limit reached (>= 100 on this business day).
    if (countOwnersRegisteredOn(registrationDate) >= 100) {
        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);
    }
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = candidate;
    owner.setRegistrationDate(registrationDate);
    owner.setCustomerCode(customerCode(owner));
    owner.setNamesakeCount(countNamesakes(owner.getFirstName(), owner.getLastName()));
    owner.setBulkSignupWarning(countOwnersRegisteredOn(registrationDate) > 80);
    owner.setHouseholdSize(countHouseholdMembers(owner) + 1);
    if (declaredMember) {
        owner.setPossibleDuplicate(false);
        owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(null);
    }
    else {
        Owner softMatch = findPossibleDuplicate(owner);
        owner.setPossibleDuplicate(softMatch != null);
        owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(softMatch == null ? null : softMatch.getId());
    }
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    AUDIT.info("owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
        owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(),
        ownerMapper.membershipLevel(owner));
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```

### Order of validations / side-effects inside `addOwner`

1. **`@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")`** — requires role `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN` (see `Roles`), enforced by Spring method security. On failure throws `AccessDeniedException`.
2. **Email**: `normalizeEmail` (lines 283-300) — blank → null; else lower-cases, checks `EMAIL_PATTERN`, rejects disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) → `400` on failure.
3. **Postcode**: `normalizePostcode` (lines 313-331) — blank → null; must be 4 digits; if city maps to a known region (`OwnerMapper.CITY_REGION`), must fall in that region's range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) → `400` on failure.
4. **Address**: `normalizeAddress` (lines 339-356) — trims/collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST/RD/AVE`; blank → `400`; normalized form written back to DTO.
5. **City capacity**: `countOwnersInCity` (lines 523-528) — `>= 50` existing owners in city → `409 CONFLICT`.
6. **Telephone**: `toE164` (lines 385-419) — strips separators, assumes `+61` when no country code, enforces 8-15 digits and per-country national-number length → `400` on failure; normalized value written back.
7. **Mapping to entity**: `ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` produces the `Owner` candidate.
8. **Identity duplicate**: `identityContact` (lines 365-369) compares `telephone|email` against all existing owners → `409 CONFLICT`.
9. **Household duplicate**: `ownerMapper.householdId` — if a household already exists and `sharesHousehold` is not true → `409 CONFLICT`.
10. **Registration date**: default to today; future date → `400`; rolled to next business day via `toBusinessDay` (lines 544-550).
11. **Daily limit**: `countOwnersRegisteredOn` (lines 534-538) — `>= 100` → `429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS`.
12. **Derived fields set on the entity**: `customerCode` (lines 475-479, uses `deriveRegion` 487-498 and `sha256HexUpper` 504-517), `namesakeCount` (`countNamesakes` 426-433), `bulkSignupWarning` (`> 80` today), `householdSize` (`countHouseholdMembers` 440-445, +1), `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` (`findPossibleDuplicate` 454-465).
13. **Persist**: `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`.
14. **Side-effect**: `AUDIT.info(...)` log line (uses `ownerMapper.membershipLevel`).
15. **Response**: map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location` header, return `201 CREATED`.

Note: every one of the `findAllOwners()`-based checks (steps 5, 8, 9, 11, 12) issues a full table read through the service/repository each time.

---

## 2. The request DTO and its Bean Validation annotations

**File:** `/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerFieldsDto.java`

